---
import DocsApiTable from './DocsApiTable.astro';
---
  <p>These options implement the exported <code>AttachmentOptions</code> type. Only <code>host</code> is required.</p>
  <DocsApiTable label="Shared creation options">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Default</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>host</code><p>An HTML container already on the page, with CSS position other than static. It must contain the target in the same document; it cannot be the target itself.</p></th><td><code>HTMLElement</code></td><td>Required</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>clock</code><p>Use manual for your code or GSAP to control time; auto advances time automatically. The older spelling ambient remains supported.</p></th><td><code>'manual' | 'auto' | 'ambient'</code></td><td><code>'manual'</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>motion</code><p>respect suppresses output under reduced motion. static always renders a still effect at time zero, under either preference.</p></th><td><code>'respect' | 'static'</code></td><td><code>'respect'</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>seed</code><p>Fixed random seed. Reuses the same pattern at a given time and settings on the same captured target; it is not a randomness amount or a cross-device pixel guarantee.</p></th><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>0</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>time</code><p>Initial effect time in seconds. Negative values are accepted.</p></th><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>0</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>intensity</code><p>Initial effect strength. Accepted values clamp to 0–1; the visual response depends on the effect.</p></th><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>1</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </DocsApiTable>
  <p>Numeric attachment options must be finite and representable as float32. Invalid values throw before clamping. To change a creation option other than <code>time</code> or <code>intensity</code>, dispose the attachment and create a replacement.</p>
  <p class="docs-api-note">Only one effect can use a target at a time. Invalid host relationships and overlapping targets throw synchronously. Dispose the existing effect before attaching to the same target, its ancestor or a descendant. This restriction describes the element tree, not arbitrary visual overlap.</p>
